        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{9}$",
          "worked": "There are $48+60+20+25=153$ items, of which $48+20=68$ have green wrapping.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{green wrapping})&=\\frac{68}{153}\\\\P(\\text{green wrapping})&=\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "an item with green wrapping given that it is a chocolate.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4}{9}$",
          "worked": "Restrict the sample space to the $48+60=108$ chocolates. Of these, $48$ have green wrapping.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{green wrapping}\\mid\\text{chocolate})&=\\frac{48}{108}\\\\P(\\text{green wrapping}\\mid\\text{chocolate})&=\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
